# SMD MkDocs Documentation Site [SPEC:SMD-MKDOCS]

> A MkDocs plugin that transforms SMD files into an internally hyperlinked documentation site where every bracketed ID is a clickable link, every relationship is traversable, and the semantic graph that AI reads via grep is visible to humans via browser.

---

## 1. Problem Statement

### [SD-PROBLEM] The Traversal Gap

SMD files are designed for dual readership: human-readable Markdown AND machine-parseable semantic structure. An Intelligence traverses the graph by grepping for `[DP-CIO-5]`, reading the file, following `depends-on` to the next spec, reading relationship sections to find edges. Three tool calls, sub-second.

A human opens the same file in a Markdown renderer and sees flat text. Bracketed IDs are inert strings. `depends-on` lists are text, not links. Relationship sections declare edges that go nowhere. The semantic structure — the thing that makes SMD more than Markdown — is invisible.

- rationale: The gap is not in the format (SMD is well-designed for both audiences) but in the rendering toolchain. Standard Markdown renderers discard the semantic layer because they don't know it exists.
- constraint: The solution must preserve SMD's property of being valid Markdown. The plugin adds navigation ON TOP of standard rendering, it does not replace it.

### [SD-PROBLEM-PRIMER] Prior Design Work

A design primer exists at `ux_composer/specs/PRIMER-smd-navigator.md` documenting working knowledge from authoring 8 SMD specs and running spec-gap-analyzer against them. That primer informs this spec.

Full knowledge navigator specs exist at `~/icpd/22-knowledge-navigator.smd` (system architecture) and `~/icpd/23-knowledge-navigator-style.smd` (visual design). Those are future scope — this spec builds the foundation they will extend.

- external-ref: Existing d3.js navigator work at `~/icpd/src/navigator/` (Vue/Svelte, partially complete)

---

## 2. Architecture

### [SD-ARCH] MkDocs + Material + Plugin

MkDocs with Material theme provides ~60% of the navigator for free: dark mode, navigation tabs, full-text search, sidebar TOC, admonitions, and native Mermaid diagram support. The custom `mkdocs-smd` Python plugin adds the semantic layer.

- rationale: SMD is valid Markdown by design (SMD v2 specification, Section 2). Building a custom renderer from scratch would reimplement what MkDocs already does. The plugin architecture lets us add semantic navigation without owning the rendering stack.
- constraint: Python — matches ComposeIO ecosystem. Plugin parser can share code with spec-gap-analyzer and smd-linter in the future.

### [SD-ARCH-PLUGIN] Plugin Structure

```
mkdocs-smd-plugin/
  setup.py                    # Package entry point
  mkdocs_smd/
    __init__.py               # MkDocs plugin class (hook registration)
    parser.py                 # Regex extraction: nodes, properties, edges, refs
    indexer.py                # Cross-document [ID] -> (page, anchor, title, first_property)
    rewriter.py               # Markdown rewriting: [IDs] -> links, frontmatter -> nav
    traceability.py           # Relationship chain -> matrix page generation
    graph_exporter.py         # Emit graph.json for d3.js consumer (phase 2)
```

- compliance: Plugin MUST register as a standard MkDocs plugin via `entry_points` in setup.py
- compliance: All state between hooks MUST be stored on the plugin instance, not in module globals

### [SD-ARCH-HOOKS] MkDocs Hook Lifecycle

The plugin uses three MkDocs hooks in sequence:

**`on_files` (build start):** Scan all `.smd` files in the docs directory. Run parser on each. Build the cross-document index. Generate traceability matrix pages. Emit `graph.json`.

**`on_page_markdown` (per page):** Rewrite the Markdown before MkDocs renders it:
1. Resolve `[BRACKETED-IDS]` in prose to hyperlinks with hover tooltips
2. Transform frontmatter `depends-on` into navigation links
3. Transform relationship sections into linked references
4. Transform causal graph declarations into Mermaid diagrams
5. Render `scope` and `boundary` as banner admonitions

**`on_page_context` (per page):** Inject "referenced by" data — reverse-lookup from the index showing every page/node that references nodes defined on this page.

- compliance: Hook execution order MUST be: on_files (once) -> on_page_markdown (per page) -> on_page_context (per page). The indexer must complete before any rewriting begins.

---

## 3. Parser

### [SD-PARSER] Regex Extraction

SMD is deliberately regex-friendly. The parser extracts five element types using patterns from the SMD v2.0 specification:

| Element | Pattern | Yields |
|---------|---------|--------|
| Document header | `^#\s+(.+)\s+\[([A-Z][A-Z0-9]+):([A-Z0-9_\-]+)\]$` | title, doc_type, doc_id |
| Node header | `^(#{2,4})\s+\[([A-Z][A-Z0-9_\-]+)\]\s+(.+)$` | level, node_id, title |
| Property | `^-\s+([a-z][a-z0-9_\-]*)\s*:\s+(.+)$` | key, value |
| Bracketed reference | `\[([A-Z][A-Z0-9_\-]+)\]` | ref_id |
| Causal declaration | `\[([A-Z][A-Z0-9_\-]+)\]\s+(CAUSES\|ENABLES\|PREVENTS\|CASCADES_TO\|PRECONDITION_FOR)\s+\[([A-Z][A-Z0-9_\-]+)\]` | source, edge_type, target |

- compliance: Parser MUST handle YAML frontmatter via PyYAML or ruamel.yaml, not regex
- compliance: Parser MUST build section hierarchy from heading levels (h2 contains h3 contains h4) to infer CONTAINS edges
- compliance: Parser MUST extract the first property value for each node (used in hover tooltips)

### [SD-PARSER-SCOPE] What the Parser Does NOT Do

The parser extracts structure for navigation. It does NOT:
- Validate SMD format correctness (that is the smd-linter's job)
- Analyze semantic content quality (that is smd-corpus-analyzer's job)
- Modify source .smd files (read-only)

---

## 4. Indexer

### [SD-INDEX] Cross-Document Reference Index

The indexer builds a dict mapping every bracketed ID to its location and metadata:

```python
index: dict[str, NodeEntry]
# where NodeEntry contains:
#   page: str          — relative path to the MkDocs page
#   anchor: str        — HTML anchor (slugified node ID)
#   title: str         — node title text
#   first_property: str — first property value (for tooltip)
#   doc_type: str      — SPEC, AMEND, SYSTEM
#   doc_id: str        — document-level ID
```

- compliance: Index MUST be built from ALL `.smd` files before any page rewriting occurs
- compliance: Index MUST handle ID collisions by preferring the definition site (node header) over reference sites (prose mentions)
- compliance: Document-level IDs (`SPEC:CIO-BUS-PROTOCOL`) and node-level IDs (`BP-MSG-FIELDS`) MUST both be indexed

### [SD-INDEX-REVERSE] Reverse Reference Index

A second index maps each node ID to the set of pages/nodes that reference it:

```python
reverse_index: dict[str, list[ReferenceEntry]]
# where ReferenceEntry contains:
#   page: str          — page containing the reference
#   node_id: str|None  — enclosing node (if reference is inside a node section)
#   context: str       — brief surrounding text
```

- rationale: Powers the "referenced by" sidebar on each page. When reading `[DP-CIO-5]`, you can see everywhere it's cited across the corpus.

---

## 5. Rewriter

### [SD-REWRITE] Markdown Transformation Rules

The rewriter modifies page Markdown before MkDocs renders it to HTML. Transformations in order:

### [SD-REWRITE-REFS] Bracketed ID Resolution

Every `[BRACKETED-ID]` in prose that exists in the index becomes a hyperlink:

```markdown
<!-- Input -->
See [DP-CIO-5] for the rationale.

<!-- Output -->
See [DP-CIO-5](../00-composeio-design-principles/#dp-cio-5 "Explicit State Engine — State machines are defined in config, not code"){.smd-ref} for the rationale.
```

- compliance: References to IDs NOT in the index MUST be left as-is (they may be forward references to unloaded documents, not errors)
- compliance: Self-references (ID referencing its own definition on the same page) MUST link to the anchor but not open a new page
- compliance: References inside code blocks and code fences MUST NOT be rewritten

### [SD-REWRITE-FRONTMATTER] Frontmatter Navigation

`depends-on` entries become a navigation banner at the top of the page:

```markdown
!!! abstract "Dependencies"
    [SPEC:CIO-BUS-PROTOCOL](../01-composeio-bus-protocol/) | [SPEC:CIO-APP](../08-composeio-app-framework/)
```

`scope` becomes the page subtitle. `boundary` becomes a collapsed admonition.

- compliance: Frontmatter MUST be consumed by the plugin and NOT rendered as raw YAML

### [SD-REWRITE-RELATIONSHIPS] Relationship Section Links

Relationship section entries become hyperlinked:

```markdown
<!-- Input -->
- depends-on: [SPEC:CIO-BUS-PROTOCOL] (transport interface)

<!-- Output -->
- **depends-on**: [SPEC:CIO-BUS-PROTOCOL](../01-composeio-bus-protocol/ "ComposeIO Bus Protocol"){.smd-rel} — transport interface
```

### [SD-REWRITE-CAUSAL] Causal Graph Visualization

Causal graph sections with `[A] CAUSES [B]` declarations are transformed into Mermaid diagrams:

```markdown
<!-- Input -->
[DP-CIO-1] CAUSES [CXC-DUAL-BUS]
[CXC-DUAL-BUS] ENABLES [CXC-CROSSOVER]

<!-- Output -->
```mermaid
graph LR
    DP-CIO-1["DP-CIO-1"] --> |CAUSES| CXC-DUAL-BUS["CXC-DUAL-BUS"]
    CXC-DUAL-BUS["CXC-DUAL-BUS"] --> |ENABLES| CXC-CROSSOVER["CXC-CROSSOVER"]
    click DP-CIO-1 "../00-composeio-design-principles/#dp-cio-1"
    click CXC-DUAL-BUS "../page/#cxc-dual-bus"
    click CXC-CROSSOVER "../page/#cxc-crossover"
`` `
```

- compliance: Mermaid node labels MUST be the bracketed ID (not the full title — too long for graph readability)
- compliance: Mermaid click handlers MUST navigate to the node definition page/anchor
- rationale: Material for MkDocs renders Mermaid natively as interactive SVG. No custom JS needed.

### [SD-REWRITE-REFBY] Referenced-By Sidebar

Each page gets an injected section (via `on_page_context` or appended Markdown) showing reverse references:

```markdown
---
## Referenced By
| ID | From | Context |
|----|------|---------|
| [DP-CIO-5](link) | node-red-integration | "Per [DP-CIO-5], state validation..." |
| [DP-CIO-5](link) | widget-renderers | "Implements [DP-CIO-5] via RendererContext" |
```

---

## 6. Traceability

### [SD-TRACE] Relationship Chain Matrices

The traceability generator scans the parsed corpus for directional relationship chains and produces auto-generated matrix pages.

### [SD-TRACE-PATTERN] Chain Detection

ComposeIO specs follow a recurring pattern: Design Principles → Derived Constraints → Anti-patterns. The generator detects these chains from:

1. **Explicit causal edges**: `[DP-CIO-1] CAUSES [CXC-DUAL-BUS]`
2. **Property references**: `- derives-from: [DP-CIO-1]` or `- see-also: [DP-CIO-1]`
3. **Structural inference**: Anti-pattern sections that reference the principle they guard against

### [SD-TRACE-MATRIX] Matrix Output

Generated as a Markdown page (added to MkDocs nav):

```markdown
# Traceability: Design Principles

| Principle | Derived Constraints | Anti-patterns | Specs Referencing |
|-----------|-------------------|---------------|-------------------|
| [DP-CIO-1](link) | [CXC-DUAL-BUS](link), [BP-SCOPE](link) | [AP-CXC-1](link) | 3 specs |
| [DP-CIO-5](link) | [CS-STATE](link) | [AP-CXC-3](link) | 5 specs |
| [DP-CIO-7](link) | — | — | 1 spec |
```

- rationale: Makes coverage gaps visible at a glance. A principle with no derived constraints is aspirational. A constraint with no anti-pattern has no guardrail. A principle referenced by zero specs is disconnected from the corpus.
- compliance: Matrix pages MUST be regenerated on every build (not cached)
- compliance: Empty cells (no constraints, no anti-patterns) MUST be rendered as `—` not hidden — gaps are information

### [SD-TRACE-CUSTOM] Extensible Chain Types

The traceability generator is not hardcoded to the principles → constraints → anti-patterns chain. Any typed relationship chain can produce a matrix:

- `SPEC → AMEND` (which amendments modify which specs)
- `depends-on` chains (transitive dependency graph as a table)
- `CAUSES/ENABLES` chains (causal propagation paths)

- compliance: The generator MUST accept chain type configuration, not assume a fixed set

---

## 7. d3.js Graph Explorer (Phase 2)

### [SD-GRAPH] Corpus-Level Visualization

- phase: 2
- status: specified, not yet delegation-ready

The graph explorer provides a "zoom out" view that per-page Mermaid diagrams cannot: seeing 50+ nodes and their cross-document relationships at once as an interactive force-directed graph.

### [SD-GRAPH-DATA] Graph Export

The plugin's indexer emits a `graph.json` file alongside the MkDocs site containing:

```json
{
  "nodes": [
    {"id": "DP-CIO-1", "title": "Bus-Centric Architecture", "doc": "design-principles", "type": "principle"},
    {"id": "CXC-DUAL-BUS", "title": "Dual Bus Architecture", "doc": "composer-arch", "type": "constraint"}
  ],
  "edges": [
    {"source": "DP-CIO-1", "target": "CXC-DUAL-BUS", "type": "CAUSES"},
    {"source": "SPEC:CIO-RENDERERS", "target": "SPEC:CIO-BUS-PROTOCOL", "type": "depends-on"}
  ]
}
```

- compliance: graph.json MUST be emitted during `on_files` alongside the site build
- compliance: Node types MUST be inferred from prefix registry (principles, constraints, anti-patterns, modules, etc.)

### [SD-GRAPH-UI] Interactive Graph Page

A dedicated page in the MkDocs site loads `graph.json` and renders via d3.js force-directed layout:

- **Click node** → navigate to the MkDocs page/anchor for that node
- **Hover node** → tooltip with title + first property
- **Filter by edge type** — show only CAUSES, only depends-on, only CONTAINS, etc.
- **Filter by document** — isolate one spec's nodes and their external edges
- **Color by node type** — principles, constraints, anti-patterns, modules visually distinct
- **Zoom/pan** — standard d3.js interaction

### [SD-GRAPH-EXISTING] Existing Work

Partial d3.js implementation exists at `~/icpd/src/navigator/` (Vue/Svelte, d3, dagre). Phase 2 should evaluate this work for reuse before building from scratch.

- constraint: The graph page must integrate cleanly into the MkDocs site (as a custom page or iframe), not require a separate server
- see-also: Full knowledge navigator specs at `~/icpd/22-knowledge-navigator.smd` and `~/icpd/23-knowledge-navigator-style.smd` for future feature scope

---

## 8. Knowledge Navigator (Future)

### [SD-KNAV] Full Interactive Navigation

- phase: future
- status: scope-setting only — see `~/icpd/22-knowledge-navigator.smd` for full spec

The knowledge navigator extends the d3.js graph with:

- View modes: Mind Map, Hierarchy, Flow, Change Impact
- Composable overlays: Test Coverage, Contradictions, Retirement candidates
- Role-gated access (different views for different audiences)
- Backend API for live corpus queries

This is specified in `~/icpd/22-knowledge-navigator.smd` and `~/icpd/23-knowledge-navigator-style.smd`. Those specs become actionable once phase 1 (rewriter + traceability) and phase 2 (d3.js graph) are proven.

- constraint: Phase 1 and 2 MUST be designed so the knowledge navigator can extend them, not replace them

---

## 9. Site Configuration

### [SD-SITE-CONFIG] MkDocs Configuration

```yaml
site_name: ComposeIO Specification Corpus
theme:
  name: material
  palette:
    scheme: slate          # Dark mode default
  features:
    - navigation.tabs      # Top-level spec categories as tabs
    - navigation.sections  # Collapsible sidebar sections
    - search.highlight     # Highlight search terms in results
    - content.tooltips     # Native tooltip support

plugins:
  - search
  - mkdocs-smd            # The custom plugin

markdown_extensions:
  - pymdownx.superfences:
      custom_fences:
        - name: mermaid
          class: mermaid
          format: !!python/name:pymdownx.superfences.fence_code_format
  - admonition
  - pymdownx.details
  - attr_list             # For .smd-ref CSS class on rewritten links
```

### [SD-SITE-NAV] Navigation Structure

Auto-generated from the docs directory structure. Each `.smd` file becomes a page. Suggested grouping:

```yaml
nav:
  - Platform:
    - spec/00-composeio-design-principles.smd
    - spec/01-composeio-bus-protocol.smd
    - spec/02-composeio-config-schema.smd
    - ...
  - Composer:
    - ux_composer/specs/00-...smd
    - ...
  - Amendments:
    - spec/01-amendment-*.smd
    - spec/02-amendment-*.smd
  - Traceability:
    - _generated/traceability-principles.md
    - _generated/traceability-dependencies.md
  - Graph: graph.md        # Phase 2
```

- compliance: Navigation grouping SHOULD be configurable in mkdocs.yml, not hardcoded in the plugin

---

## 10. Compliance Summary

### [SD-COMPLIANCE] Phase 1 Requirements

| ID | Requirement | Testable Criterion |
|----|-------------|-------------------|
| SD-C1 | Every bracketed ID in prose resolves to a hyperlink if the target exists in the index | Click any `[ID]` → navigates to definition |
| SD-C2 | Hover on a resolved reference shows title + first property | Tooltip appears within 200ms |
| SD-C3 | `depends-on` frontmatter rendered as navigation links | Links at top of page, all clickable |
| SD-C4 | Relationship section entries are hyperlinked | Both `[ID]` references in relationship lines are clickable |
| SD-C5 | Causal graph sections produce Mermaid diagrams | Diagram renders, nodes are clickable |
| SD-C6 | Referenced-by section appears on pages with inbound references | Table shows all pages referencing nodes on this page |
| SD-C7 | Traceability matrix auto-generated for principle chains | Matrix page exists in nav, all cells linked |
| SD-C8 | Traceability gaps visible as empty cells | Principles with no constraints show `—` |
| SD-C9 | References in code blocks are NOT rewritten | Code samples preserve original text |
| SD-C10 | Unresolved references left as-is | No broken links for IDs not in corpus |
| SD-C11 | Full-text search works across all SMD pages | Material search returns results from any page |
| SD-C12 | Site builds from SMD files without modifying them | Source .smd files unchanged after build |

### [SD-COMPLIANCE-P2] Phase 2 Requirements

| ID | Requirement | Testable Criterion |
|----|-------------|-------------------|
| SD-C13 | graph.json emitted on build | File exists in site output |
| SD-C14 | Graph page renders all nodes and edges | Visual inspection: node count matches index |
| SD-C15 | Click graph node navigates to MkDocs page | Navigation occurs on click |
| SD-C16 | Filter by edge type works | Toggling filter hides/shows edges |
| SD-C17 | Filter by document works | Toggling filter isolates nodes |

